-- ============================================================================
-- PD4 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Rod Pump Design, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: WHAT THE CARD HIDES. Three of its graded fields come
-- from balanceUnit, which cannot be reached at all without first solving the
-- card and which is the only place the gearbox is sized. One comes from the
-- modified Goodman line, the check that decides whether the string survives
-- the card. Two come from diagnoseCard, the Gibbs harmonic solver, which is
-- handed the surface half of the predicted card and asked what the pump was
-- doing. Those two share no code path with the march that made the card, so
-- the gap between them is a measurement of the engine against itself.
--
-- THE TIER OPENS ON THE RESULT THAT REFRAMES THE WHOLE COURSE: THE REPORTED
-- LOADS ARE NOT THE LOADS COMPUTED. predictCard marches at the Courant step,
-- 4228 steps in a cycle on the capstone well, and accumulates the tension
-- envelope over every one of them. It then DECIMATES the surface card to 184
-- points and reads the peak and the minimum polished rod load off THAT
-- SUBSAMPLE. The peak comes back 403.39 lb low. The minimum comes back 2.83
-- TIMES the load the march actually computed, because a minimum is where a
-- coarse sample is least likely to land on the extreme. Raising `cardSamples`
-- alone recovers both, and runRodPumpDesign exposes NEITHER `cardSamples` NOR
-- `nodes`, so a studio user gets the subsampled pair and no way to ask for the
-- other.
--
-- AND THE LOADS ARE NOT CONVERGED, WHILE THE PLUNGER STROKE IS. Across 120,
-- 240, 480 and 960 nodes the plunger stroke moves 0.041044911 in, four
-- hundredths of one percent, while the peak load moves 967.98 lb and the
-- minimum 1108.07 lb, 4.2 and 34.8 percent. At 240 nodes the march does not
-- reach a repeating cycle in the twenty strokes it is allowed and returns
-- `notPeriodic`, so the sequence is not even monotone in convergence. The
-- consequence the tier must state plainly: a worst rod loading of 105.16,
-- 106.34, 104.60, 109.06, 111.23 percent across a 10.6 to 12.2 spm sweep is
-- NOT monotonic, and the dip is SMALLER than the grid spread on the load it is
-- built from. That is numerical noise, not a speed at which the rods unload,
-- and a course that taught the dip as a result would be teaching the artefact.
--
-- AN INPUT BEING ACCEPTED IS NOT AN INPUT BEING READ. runRodPumpDesign
-- destructures a structural unbalance, a crank offset and a kinematics object,
-- lists all three in its own documented input list, and references none of
-- them in its body. Its output is BIT IDENTICAL with them and without them,
-- which is provable by strict equality rather than by tolerance. Hand the same
-- two to balanceUnit and the peak torque moves four percent. The reader's test
-- is not whether the call was accepted. It is which function was asked.
--
-- A MISCONCEPTION THE MODULE HEADER ITSELF NAMES. The counterbalance effect is
-- the moment divided by the TORQUE FACTOR a quarter turn past the bottom of
-- the stroke, where the counterweight moment peaks, plus the structural
-- unbalance. It is NOT the moment divided by the beam's front arm: the torque
-- factor at the quarter turn is not an arm length, and using the arm
-- understates the effect by roughly a factor of two.
--
-- WHAT THIS TIER MUST NOT OVERSTATE. None of the seven findings this wave
-- recorded is oracled, and that is not an oversight. The independent oracle
-- holds the wave equation to 2 percent on the plunger stroke and 3 percent on
-- the minimum polished rod load, so everything smaller is invisible to it BY
-- CONSTRUCTION, and the 2.83x minimum sits inside a 3 percent gate because the
-- gate is on a different well. An oracle passing and an engine being right are
-- two statements, and knowing which one you have is the skill this tier ends on.
-- ============================================================================

values ('rodpump', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-envelope-and-the-subsample","title":"The Envelope and the Subsample","lesson_keys":["l01-what-the-march-accumulates","l02-the-card-is-decimated","l03-two-loads-from-one-object","l04-what-the-subsample-costs","l05-which-check-reads-which"]},{"key":"m02-convergence","title":"Convergence","lesson_keys":["l01-nodes-and-steps","l02-what-converges-and-what-does-not","l03-the-periodicity-flag","l04-smaller-than-the-noise","l05-what-a-sweep-cannot-resolve"]},{"key":"m03-the-counterbalance","title":"The Counterbalance","lesson_keys":["l01-what-a-counterbalance-does","l02-the-moment","l03-peak-torque","l04-what-the-balance-asserts"]},{"key":"m04-inputs-that-do-nothing","title":"Inputs That Do Nothing","lesson_keys":["l01-three-inputs-never-read","l02-proving-it-by-strict-equality","l03-what-a-fails-open-looks-like","l04-what-a-caller-may-assume"]},{"key":"m05-stress-and-diagnosis","title":"Stress and Diagnosis","lesson_keys":["l01-the-modified-goodman-line","l02-a-service-factor-is-a-judgement","l03-reading-a-measured-card","l04-the-diagnostic-against-the-design","l05-what-a-diagnosis-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
